{"name":"Red Menace","hex":"#aa2121","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red menace","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of red scare."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_menace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Scare","blocks":[{"text":"Red Scare is a form of moral panic provoked by fear of the rise of left-wing ideologies in a society, especially communism and socialism. Historically, red scares have led to mass political persecution, scapegoating, and the ousting of those in government positions who have had connections with left-wing movements. The name is derived from the red flag, a common symbol of communism and socialism."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Scare","wikidata":"Q622454"},{"title":"Red Menace (New Mexico Lobos)","blocks":[{"text":"The Red Menace is the name of the bleacher section behind the North end zone in University Stadium, the home field of the New Mexico Lobos. It is known for having some of the most-rabid fans in the Mountain West Conference."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Menace_(New_Mexico_Lobos)","wikidata":"Q7304591"},{"title":"Red Menace (Grimm)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Red Menace\" is the ninth episode and midseason premiere of season 3 of the supernatural drama television series Grimm and the 53rd episode overall, which premiered on January 3, 2014, on the cable network NBC. The episode was written by Alan DiFiore, and was directed by Allan Kroeker."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Menace_(Grimm)","wikidata":"Q25935485"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1919_Political_Cartoon_%2814759129762%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-1919_Political_Cartoon_%2814759129762%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1919_Political_Cartoon_%2814759129762%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-1919_Political_Cartoon_%2814759129762%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A political cartoon from 1919 depicting the October Revolution's impact on the Paris peace talks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1919_Political_Cartoon_(14759129762)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Come_unto_me%2C_ye_opprest.jpg/330px-Come_unto_me%2C_ye_opprest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Come_unto_me%2C_ye_opprest.jpg/330px-Come_unto_me%2C_ye_opprest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A \"European Anarchist\" attempts to destroy the Statue of Liberty in this 1919 political cartoon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACome_unto_me%2C_ye_opprest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Palmer_Bombing.jpg/330px-Palmer_Bombing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Palmer_Bombing.jpg/330px-Palmer_Bombing